  "worked_solution": "Since the line $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ is a vertical line, a perpendicular line would need to be horizontal. So, the perpendicular line must take the form $y=k$ for some value of $k.$\n\nThe perpendicular line needs to go through the point $(3,7),$ which has a $y$-coordinate of $7.$ So, the perpendicular line is $y=7.$",
